{"type": "message", "id": "1b2ddec0", "parentId": "56a61918", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T14:07:46.472Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "So the daily AQI by CBSA file only shows the \"defining\" (worst) pollutant for each day. CO is rarely the defining pollutant. This means the daily AQI by CBSA data alone cannot tell us about CO levels on days when CO is NOT the defining pollutant.\n\nFor this question, I need actual daily CO concentration data. Let me look for the EPA's daily monitoring data specifically for CO. The EPA has data files with raw daily CO measurements.\n\nLet me try to access the EPA AQS Daily Data or look for other data sources that provide CO concentrations by day.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The question says \"Carbon Monoxide Daily AQI Values in the Good (<=4.4 ppm) range\". \n\nSo I'm looking for years where the maximum daily 8-hour CO concentration stayed at or below 4.4 ppm across all three metro areas throughout the entire year. The EPA monitors CO using 8-hour averages, and the AQI standard is based on the 2nd highest 8-hour average. I need to find EPA monitoring data that shows the maximum CO concentration for each day across all sites in these areas.\n\nI could search for downloadable CO concentration data files from EPA AirData, or I might need to query the AQS API directly for the daily CO measurements in these cities.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_6902f11042a64c78a455bc90", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "EPA AQS daily CO concentration data download CSV site:epa.gov airdata"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "xiaomi/mimo-v2-omni", "usage": {"input": 1148, "output": 586, "cacheRead": 91781, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 93515, "cost": {"input": 0.0004592, "output": 0.0011719999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.00734248, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.00897368}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 177557